  "disclaimerBody": "<p>This Disclaimer is an integral part of the Terms of Service. <strong>By using the Software you acknowledge and agree to all the following. The Software requires no account; all creative data is saved on your local device by default.</strong></p><h4>1. Service Provided \"As Is\"</h4><p>The Software and its functions are provided on an \"as is\" and \"available\" basis. <strong>We have made every effort to ensure their accuracy and stability, but we make no express or implied warranty as to their correctness, timeliness, applicability, uninterruptedness, or freedom from error.</strong> You should make independent judgments and bear the risks of making decisions and creating content based thereon.</p><h4>2. No Guarantee of Rendering and Results</h4><p>The Software involves operations such as 3D modeling, graphic rendering, and animation preview. <strong>Due to differences in device performance, graphics card models, driver versions, system environments, browser differences, or third-party graphics interfaces, the actual display and export results may differ from the preview. We do not guarantee the consistency, accuracy, or fitness for a particular purpose of the rendering results.</strong></p><h4>3. Risk of Local Data Loss</h4><p><strong>Content you create is saved on your local device by default. We shall not be liable for any loss, damage, or unreadable data caused by device failure, system crash, browser cache cleaning, app uninstallation, system reset, storage corruption, or your misoperation, nor do we guarantee recoverability.</strong> Please export and back up important works regularly.</p><h4>4. Responsibility for User Content</h4><p>You are responsible for the legality and authenticity of all content you create, import, upload, or share in the Software. <strong>Disputes and liabilities arising from your content infringing the rights of others, violating laws and regulations, or causing any damage to any third party shall be borne solely by you, and we shall not bear any joint liability.</strong></p><h4>5. Third-Party Components and Links</h4><p>The Software may contain, invoke, or link to third-party open-source libraries, websites, services, or resources (such as Three.js and related WebGL components). <strong>We make no warranty as to the content, privacy policies, license terms, or service availability of third parties, nor shall we bear any liability; the risks of your interaction with third parties shall be borne by you.</strong></p><h4>6. Exported Files and Compatibility</h4><p><strong>We cannot guarantee that your exported project files, images, or models will open or be compatible in other devices, other software, or higher versions. Please keep the original files and verify their usability by yourself.</strong></p><h4>7. Force Majeure</h4><p>We shall not be liable for any service interruption, function limitation, or data loss caused by force majeure or reasons not attributable to us, such as natural disasters, wars, government actions, network attacks, power or communication interruptions, or platform policy changes.</p><h4>8. Minors</h4><p><strong>If you are a minor, please read this Disclaimer with a guardian and use the Software with their consent. The guardian shall guide the minor to use the Software in a healthy and lawful manner and bear the corresponding guardianship responsibilities.</strong></p><h4>9. Limitation of Liability</h4><p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, <strong>we shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, punitive, or consequential losses (including data loss, profit loss, and device damage) arising from the use or inability to use the Software,</strong> even if we have been advised of the possibility of such damages.</p><h4>10. Changes to this Disclaimer</h4><p><strong>This Disclaimer may be adjusted with software updates, and will be announced within the Software after the update. Your continued use is deemed acceptance of the updated content; if you do not agree, please stop using the Software.</strong></p><h4>11. Software Updates and Documentation Changes</h4><p>(1) The Software may be updated from time to time, and the functions, interface, and documentation after the update may differ from the old version; we do not guarantee complete consistency between the old and new versions.</p><p>(2) With version updates, the manual text may be revised, and notes you created based on the old manual text may not maintain the original binding relationship after the text changes; please refer to the latest version of the manual.</p>",
