  "faq.a10": "These systems have no native package—just use the Web version: touch devices (iPhone / iPad / HarmonyOS phones) automatically switch to the touch layout, and macOS / Linux desktops can open it right in the browser. Projects still sync across all three platforms.",
  "faq.a2": "The vast majority of features are exactly the same, sharing the same core engine. Differences come only from the install method, and from Android's native save/open dialogs and back key confirm. Android's \"Fullscreen\" is only a visual fullscreen that fits the status bar.",
