  "privacyBody": "<p>Cube · 3D Design Workshop (hereinafter referred to as the \"Software\" or \"we\") is an <strong>lightweight</strong> cross-platform 3D/2D scene editor provided to you by <strong>Yushichadao</strong> as an individual developer. We <strong>do not collect your personal information</strong>; your creative content and local settings are saved by default only on your own device, and there is no circumstance in which we transmit, store, or use your personal information for other purposes. By using the Software, you agree to this Policy.</p><h4>1. Account Information</h4><p><strong>The Software has no account system; you may use it without registering or logging in. We do not collect, store, or bind your username, password, email, phone number, or other account-type personal information to your identity.</strong></p><h4>2. Local Creative Data</h4><p>(1) <strong>The 3D models, scenes, sticky notes, annotations, text, and images you create are saved by default on your local device (browser storage, application sandbox, or files you export), and will not be uploaded to any server.</strong></p><p>(2) Except for the local technical processing necessary to provide local functions, we will not actively read, upload, or transmit your creative content.</p><h4>3. Third-Party SDKs</h4><p><strong>The Software will not integrate any third-party SDK that requires collecting or sharing your personal information (including analytics, crash reporting, advertising, cloud sync, social sharing, etc.). The Software only uses necessary open-source graphics libraries (such as Three.js and WebGL components) running locally, which will not transmit your personal information externally.</strong></p><h4>4. Entrustment, Sharing, Transfer, and Public Disclosure</h4><p>(1) We will not sell your personal information to any third party.</p><p>(2) <strong>Except in the following circumstances, we will not share, transfer, or publicly disclose your personal information:</strong></p><p>1. To comply with applicable laws, regulations, judicial, or regulatory requirements;</p><p>2. To protect the legitimate rights and interests of the Software, you, or the public;</p><p>3. With your prior explicit consent.</p><p>(3) Since the Software does not collect your personal information, the above circumstances generally will not occur.</p><h4>5. Data Security and Your Responsibilities</h4><p>(1) Your core creative data is mainly saved on your own local device; please keep your device properly and set a lock screen to prevent unauthorized access by others.</p><p>(2) <strong>Please export and back up important works regularly; we cannot guarantee recovery of data lost due to device damage, browser cleanup, app uninstallation, system reset, or operational errors, and the relevant risks shall be borne by you.</strong></p><p>(3) If you contact us by email, the email address you provide will only be used to reply to your question and will not be used for other purposes.</p><h4>6. Your Rights and Opt-Out</h4><p><strong>You always control your data: you may clear the cache, delete works, uninstall the app, or stop using the Software at any time.</strong></p><h4>7. Policy Updates</h4><p><strong>This Policy may be adjusted with software updates, and the updated version will be announced within the Software. Your continued use is deemed acceptance; if you do not agree, please stop using the Software.</strong></p><h4>8. Contact Us</h4><p>Developer: <strong>Yushichadao</strong><br>Contact email: <strong>yushichadao@qq.com</strong></p><h4>9. Textual Effect</h4><p>This Policy is governed by its Simplified Chinese version; if any other language version is inconsistent with this Simplified Chinese version, the Simplified Chinese version shall prevail.</p><h4>10. Update Detection</h4><p>(1) To provide you with version updates and security fixes, the Software may automatically detect whether a new version is available. This detection only requests necessary version information (such as the current version number), and does not involve, collect, or upload your creative content, notes, or any personal information.</p><p>(2) You may turn off automatic update detection in the settings, or choose not to update and continue using the current version.</p>",
